    "details": "NLnet Labs reports:\n\n> - CVE-2026-18664: IP range access control restrictions are bypassed\n>   for some unintended IP. Reported by [Qifan Zhang from Palo Alto\n>   Networks](https://qifanz.com/), [Claude](https://claude.ai) and [Ada\n>   Logics](https://adalogics.com/).\n> - CVE-2026-18916: Any remote client can denial TCP service by\n>   throttling the TCP receive window (down to 1). Reported by [akoul\n>   (Akhil Koul)](https://github.com/akoul)\n> - CVE-2026-19401: Any remote client can denial UDP service by sending\n>   a specifically crafted query with multiple DNS Cookie options.\n>   Reported by [Qifan Zhang from Palo Alto\n>   Networks](https://qifanz.com/) and\n>   [afldl](mailto:zhangph@yandex.com).\n> - CVE-2026-19538: Anyone with access to the proxy protocol port over\n>   TCP or TLS can bypass BLOCKED access control items. Reported by\n>   [Qifan Zhang from Palo Alto Networks](https://qifanz.com/).\n",
